<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/infographic-pos-fnb-checklist.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@600;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<div class="n3l-pos-fnb-checklist">
<figure class="fig">
  <header class="mast">
    <span class="eyebrow brand-eyebrow">NEXT3LABS &mdash; F&amp;B operations</span>
    <p class="display-title">The POS test that matters <span class="hi">after</span> the demo</p>
    <p class="sub">Six checks. Run them against your actual service, not a feature sheet.</p>
    <div class="mast-rule"></div>
  </header>

  <section class="scorecard" aria-label="POS selection checklist">
    <div class="scorecard-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Selection scorecard</span>
      <span class="instruction">For every answer: show it, then write down the failure path.</span>
    </div>
    <ol class="checks">
      <li class="check check--service">
        <span class="check-no">01</span>
        <div><h2>Service keeps moving</h2><p>Run a modifier, split bill, void and close. Then test the connection dropping and returning.</p></div>
        <span class="prompt">What still works?</span>
      </li>
      <li class="check check--records">
        <span class="check-no">02</span>
        <div><h2>Records survive scrutiny</h2><p>Trace a GST transaction, discount and refund from receipt to daily summary and export.</p></div>
        <span class="prompt">Can finance follow it?</span>
      </li>
      <li class="check check--outlets">
        <span class="check-no">03</span>
        <div><h2>Outlets stay consistent</h2><p>Publish a menu change, price and modifier rule. Check who can change it and how it rolls back.</p></div>
        <span class="prompt">One source of truth?</span>
      </li>
      <li class="check check--integrations">
        <span class="check-no">04</span>
        <div><h2>Integrations have a failure path</h2><p>For every connection, know what it reads, writes, updates and how exceptions are found.</p></div>
        <span class="prompt">Who notices drift?</span>
      </li>
      <li class="check check--people">
        <span class="check-no">05</span>
        <div><h2>Permissions match the floor</h2><p>Use staff PINs and defined approvals. Confirm the audit trail for voids, discounts and changes.</p></div>
        <span class="prompt">Can actions be explained?</span>
      </li>
      <li class="check check--ownership">
        <span class="check-no">06</span>
        <div><h2>Ownership extends beyond launch</h2><p>List training, devices, support, data export and the recurring work around the system.</p></div>
        <span class="prompt">What work remains?</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <figcaption class="foot">
    <span class="eyebrow">The decision rule</span>
    <strong>Do not buy the smoothest demo. Choose the clearest operating answer.</strong>
  </figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
